comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T07:32:16.381Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete strict all-status corpus of 3242 items including 2923 closed items and request-specific keyword search reviewed. No matching owner for this GitHub report. Reuse the existing parent capability and preserve closed recovery/configuration lineage."
  "2026-11-09T07:48:23.639Z","harness:codex","Negative-control evidence: new regression assertions ran against unchanged production source before the fix. The focused run failed exactly the settings-path, leading-slash source, matcher-index and strict-close-headline assertions: 4 failures and176 existing passes. Production repair preserves existing validators and sensitive input redaction."
  "2026-11-09T09:53:13.984Z","harness:codex","PR #1696 review remediation: the concise strict-close headline is independent of optional package recovery data. The immediate retry is explicitly labeled a template requiring real evidence. The existing guidance test now asserts direct placement and exactly one retry, and the real CLI preserves history on refusal."
  "2026-11-09T10:02:53.394Z","harness:codex","Large-domain review outcome: the SDK error context retains complete recovery.allowed_values, while the existing fixed JSON diagnostic ceiling can compact very large custom schemas. Text now explicitly names the complete SDK route and discloses JSON budgeting; it no longer promises that normal --output-budget controls diagnostic ceilings. A dedicated additive CLI restore contract is tracked open/unclaimed in pm-v1kspa under recovery closure, discovered from completed pm-cha95z. Default diagnostic ratchets remain intact."
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-09T10:03:50.434Z","harness:codex",A concise refusal must keep a complete headline and place its retry once at the top. Label placeholder retries as templates and do not promise optional recovery fields or an ineffective diagnostic budget override.
